# /checkout has always just bounced to /cart. With real 404s below it needs an
# explicit rule, otherwise a bookmarked /checkout would start returning 404.
/checkout   /cart   301

# Every real route is prerendered to its own HTML file by scripts/prerender.js,
# and Netlify serves a matching static file before it consults this rule. So
# this line only catches URLs that genuinely do not exist — which now return a
# real 404 instead of the old "200 OK plus a Not Found page", the thing that
# made Google treat every typo'd URL as a thin duplicate of the homepage.
/*    /404.html   404
